WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.560
A fiery prophecy, zombie pilgrims, and a poisoned
poisoner – "Wednesday" ended with such a

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.340
bang that you may have missed how the pieces
fit together.

00:00:09.193 --> 00:00:13.880
Everything happening in the explosive finale
of "Wednesday" is tied to a maniacal colonizer

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:17.029
who founded the village of Jericho named Joseph
Crackstone.

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:20.118
He is a vile and devious man who hates outcasts.

00:00:20.118 --> 00:00:23.660
Even though the outcasts lived in this part
of North America before he and his ilk ever

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.949
arrived there, he wants to eradicate them
from the face of the Earth.

00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:31.547
His prejudice sets the stage for the show's
exploration of bigotry through a fantastical lens.

00:00:31.547 --> 00:00:36.000
One of those outcasts is an ancestor of Wednesday
Addams, who also happens to look exactly like

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.709
her, named Goody Addams.

00:00:37.709 --> 00:00:41.780
Her family is killed by Crackstone, but she
escapes and vows vengeance.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.050
She kills Crackstone, curses his soul, and
puts him in a casket sealed with a blood lock

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.634
to keep him from ever returning.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:52.357
When Wednesday first visits Jericho, Sheriff
Donovan tells her exactly what he thinks of

00:00:52.357 --> 00:00:52.933
her father.

00:00:53.029 --> 00:00:55.806
"That man belongs behind bars for murder."

00:00:56.231 --> 00:01:00.550
Upon further investigation, Wednesday discovers
that when her parents were students at Nevermore,

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:03.960
Gomez was accused of killing a normie named
Garett Gates.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.080
The truth is that Garett was a descendant
of Joseph Crackstone tasked with killing everyone

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.030
at Nevermore with nightshade poisoning.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:14.190
However, Garett was so obsessed with Morticia
that he tried to kill Gomez so that he could

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.190
have her.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:19.420
During their altercation, a vial of nightshade
poison shattered in his pocket, killing him.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:23.930
Following the death of Garett, his sister
Laurel flees the country and is believed to

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:25.390
have drowned later on.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:27.750
However, Laurel Gates fakes her death.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.280
Like the rest of her family, she hates outcasts
and can't stand the fact that they built a

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.590
school for them on her ancestor's land and
killed her brother.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.290
So Laurel builds a new identity: Marilyn Thornhill.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:41.610
She returns to Jericho and manages to secure
a teaching position at Nevermore.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:45.759
The school sees having a normie on the staff
as a first step in bringing outcasts and normies

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:47.990
together, but it is all a ruse.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:51.690
Thornhill's mission from the very beginning
is to resurrect her fallen ancestor and allow

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.049
him to finish his work.

00:01:53.049 --> 00:01:57.469
This line of thinking is reminiscent of modern
racists who preach the virtues of the "good

00:01:57.469 --> 00:02:01.110
old days" -- but Thornhill takes it to the
extreme by literally bringing someone from

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.530
the old days back to achieve his bigoted goals.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:13.550
The ending of the season was prophesied around
the same time Morticia and Gomez attended

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.550
Nevermore.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:18.050
A fellow student who is a powerful seer has
a vision of the school burning.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:21.550
She recreates the image in a book that is
locked away in a library hidden in the lower

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:22.980
regions of Nevermore.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.370
It depicts a Pilgrim battling a pig-tailed
young girl.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.700
That student is so convinced that the girl
in the picture will destroy the school that

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.250
she eventually orders her son Rowan to kill
her if he sees her.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:36.780
As it turns out, though, psychic visions aren't
the most reliable when it comes to seeing

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.780
the future.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:41.470
We do see Wednesday confronting a Pilgrim,
but she isn't there to destroy the school

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:42.770
-- she's saving it.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:47.780
This, again, plays into the idea that the
way we see the world can be obscured by our biases.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.470
As Morticia informs Wednesday, psychic visions
are personalized.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.250
If you're optimistic, or a dove, you see happy
visions.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.190
If you're pessimistic, or a raven, you see
doom and gloom.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:00.900
The woman who prophesied the final battle
must have been a raven because she assumed

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.589
disaster was coming when it was actually salvation.

00:03:04.262 --> 00:03:08.500
Nevermore was created to be a safe haven where
outcasts can learn and socialize without the

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.130
fear of being discriminated against.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:14.709
Of course, if you put enough people together,
cliques and social groups start to form.

00:03:14.709 --> 00:03:16.470
Such is the case when Wednesday arrives.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:20.410
While everyone there is considered to be strange
and different, they still more or less interact

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.000
the way normies do.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.441
Wednesday is too weird even for them.

00:03:23.441 --> 00:03:26.230
That doesn't mean she's incapable of making
friends, however.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:30.860
She eventually finds a group of her own; her
roommate Enid is a werewolf who can't transform.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:34.080
Eugene spends all his time with bees and has
zero friends.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.110
Xavier grew up rich with a famous father,
but he's nothing like him.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:42.379
Even Bianca, the coolest of the cool kids,
doesn't quite fit in because she's a siren.

00:03:42.379 --> 00:03:46.019
Her voice can control people so she never
knows if the people around her genuinely like

00:03:46.019 --> 00:03:49.250
her or are compelled by her voice to do what
she says.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.129
This unifies them and helps create the perfect
team to stand up to Thornhill and Crackstone.

00:03:54.209 --> 00:03:58.049
We eventually learn that Goody Addams founded
a secret society known as the Nightshades

00:03:58.049 --> 00:04:02.470
in the early days of Nevermore to protect
outcasts from vindictive normies.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.530
Wednesday discovers the location of their
headquarters by matching the watermark on

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.670
the drawing of the prophecy with the statue
of Edgar Allan Poe and solving a riddle.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:13.840
As it turns out, the society still exists
and they invite Wednesday to join them.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.250
She declines, because even a secret society
is too social for her.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:20.500
Still, the fact that she was able to discover
them earns her some points.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.380
They don't all become her friends exactly,
but when she informs them of the fight that

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:28.680
is about to take place, they stand with her
to protect Nevermore and outcasts in general.

00:04:29.508 --> 00:04:33.010
When Wednesday arrives at Nevermore, there's
a monster killing people.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:36.550
The sheriff has been telling everyone it's
a bear, but bears don't remove body parts

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:37.550
and leave with them.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:39.130
"Tell them a bear is back."

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:40.868
"You don't really believe that, sheriff."

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:41.857
"No, I don't."

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:46.570
Through her investigation, Wednesday discovers
the monster is called a Hyde.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:51.340
These beasts are human, but transform when
triggered by traumatic events or chemical injections.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.645
The identity of the Hyde is the main mystery
carrying the series.

00:04:54.645 --> 00:04:59.030
Hydes are tied to the people who liberate
them, considering them to be their masters.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:03.030
Thornhill knows this, and she also knows that
the sheriff's son Tyler is a Hyde.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:07.343
Following the death of his mother, Thornhill
manipulates him and becomes a surrogate parental figure.

00:05:07.343 --> 00:05:11.550
She then chains him to a cave, injects him
with her elixir, and forces him to transform

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:15.833
into a Hyde to kill people and steal their
body parts to help her resurrect Crackstone.

00:05:16.613 --> 00:05:20.509
Like many of the characters in this show,
Wednesday's perky and colorful roommate Enid

00:05:20.509 --> 00:05:22.220
is at war with herself.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:25.600
On the one hand, she seems to get along with
most of the kids at school and always has

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:30.050
a sunny disposition, but she is incapable
of wolfing out and is ashamed of that.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.140
For most of the show the most that changes
is her nails.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:36.800
She's worried that her inability to transform
will lead to her family disowning her.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.169
If she isn't part of a pack, werewolf society
will shun her and she will die alone.

00:05:41.169 --> 00:05:43.220
This fear drives most of her decisions.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:47.080
However, things start to change when she stands
up to her mother and proclaims she is her

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.080
own person.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.819
From that point on, she stops operating out
of fear and begins acting out of love.

00:05:51.819 --> 00:05:56.250
During the blood moon, when Nevermore is under
attack, she finally wolfs out, subduing Tyler

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.347
in his Hyde form and protecting Wednesday.

00:05:59.176 --> 00:06:00.176
"Enid?"

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:06.199
The Severus Snape in this "Harry Potter" pastiche
is Principal Weems.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:09.490
Although she is a major antagonist in the
series, she isn't the villain viewers are

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:12.160
led to think she'd be upon first encountering
her.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:16.720
In fact, every decision she makes was meant
to protect Wednesday, Nevermore, and outcasts

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:17.780
in general.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:21.080
She wants to make sure outcasts are never
seen as evil or dangerous so they would be

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.860
accepted by normies.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:27.190
What's so tragic about this is the fact that
her memories of Nevermore aren't the rosiest.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:31.271
While Morticia and Gomez remember Nevermore
being the greatest years of their lives, she

00:06:31.271 --> 00:06:33.830
recalls mostly disappointment and loneliness.

00:06:34.139 --> 00:06:37.242
"Such good times we had, didn't we Larissa?"

00:06:38.206 --> 00:06:40.494
"Some of us better than others."

00:06:40.686 --> 00:06:44.500
She has every reason to be the villain, but
she sees the good in people and that drives

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.090
her to always do what she believes is the
right thing.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:51.440
Yes, Wednesday and her friends save the school
from Thornhill and Crackstone, but Weems dedicates

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.940
her life to protecting Nevermore -- and that
makes her a true hero.

00:06:55.904 --> 00:07:00.389
Eugene is a stereotypical nerd who is so isolated
from his peers that the mere fact that his

00:07:00.389 --> 00:07:04.630
classmates are willing to visit his beekeeping
sanctuary makes him so excited he essentially

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:06.060
pledges his life to them.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:09.610
It would be easy to write him off as desperate
for companionship, but it's a little more

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.449
complicated than that.

00:07:11.449 --> 00:07:15.081
Eugene doesn't just help Wednesday with her
investigation because he wants a friend; he

00:07:15.081 --> 00:07:18.340
does so because he believes in his own buzzy
moral code.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:20.009
"Snitches get stung.

00:07:20.009 --> 00:07:21.500
It's hive code."

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:26.220
Basically, Eugene understands that every bee
in a hive works together to serve and protect

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.220
the queen.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:31.530
He is so in tune with these creatures that
he adapts their social structure to his own life.

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:35.940
During the Poe Cup, Wednesday has a vision
when touching Joseph Crackstone's crypt.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:38.692
In it, she is visited by her ancestor Goody,
who tells her:

00:07:38.808 --> 00:07:40.212
"You are the key."

00:07:40.771 --> 00:07:43.979
You might think that this is a metaphor, but
nope — it's literal.

00:07:43.979 --> 00:07:48.199
After all, Goody trapped Crackstone's body
in a casket sealed with a blood lock.

00:07:48.199 --> 00:07:52.039
As Thornhill explains in the final episode,
the only way to open it is to spill the blood

00:07:52.039 --> 00:07:54.479
of an Addams on the night of a blood moon.

00:07:54.479 --> 00:07:58.030
Thornhill sacrifices Wednesday and successfully
resurrects Crackstone.

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:01.229
However, that's not the only key Goody was
talking about.

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:04.699
Wednesday is also the only person who can
vanquish Crackstone for good by stabbing him

00:08:04.699 --> 00:08:05.699
in his heart.

00:08:05.699 --> 00:08:09.389
As she lies there dying, the spirit of Goody
passes through her thanks to her necklace

00:08:09.389 --> 00:08:13.910
and heals her wounds, freeing her to face
Crackstone and end his reign of terror forever.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:19.610
The town of Jericho serves as a visual metaphor
for the division happening in the series.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:24.501
It's a quaint town built on stolen land with
a massive school meant for outcasts looming over it.

00:08:24.501 --> 00:08:28.270
Although the money Nevermore brings into the
town keeps it thriving, the citizens there

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.810
hate the fact that weirdos are living on "their
land."

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:34.899
They have an amusement park called Pilgrim
World that teaches people all about the early

00:08:34.899 --> 00:08:36.270
days of the town's settlement.

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:40.360
It is mentioned in the series itself that
this worship of Pilgrims ignores the genocide

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:42.849
of native people and whitewashes history.

00:08:42.849 --> 00:08:46.290
Beyond paying lip service to this, however,
the show examines this dichotomy through a

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.790
visual metaphor.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:51.780
By aligning themselves with the idealized
and inaccurate depiction of pilgrims, the

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:55.320
town of Jericho makes a clear statement that
they believe natives don't deserve to exist

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:56.420
on their land.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:00.570
The land Nevermore was built on didn't belong
to Joseph Crackstone -- it was reclaimed by

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.630
the outcasts he tried to annihilate.

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:07.269
The final showdown between Wednesday and Crackstone
seems like an intentional comment on colonization

00:09:07.269 --> 00:09:11.420
as it is literally the descendant of a long
line of outcasts, Wednesday, who battles an

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:13.163
actual colonizer, Crackstone.

00:09:14.217 --> 00:09:18.480
In the end, we find out Tyler was the Hyde,
learn that Thornhill was controlling him,

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:20.380
and finally see Crackstone destroyed.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.850
Also, Wednesday learns the importance of hugging.

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:26.050
She even accepts a dreaded cell phone to stay
in touch with everyone.

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:30.090
It seems like everything is wrapped up nice
and neat -- until the final scene.

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:34.640
As paramedics transport Tyler to the hospital,
he begins transforming into Hyde form, suggesting

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:36.570
that we haven't seen the end of him.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:39.050
Additionally, there is still the question
of Wednesday's stalker.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:43.370
When examining a music box found in Laurel
Gates' room, she finds a secret compartment

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:44.850
with photos of herself.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.120
Clearly, someone has been following her and
taking snapshots.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:52.040
The easy assumption is that it was Miss Thornhill,
but if that is the case, why does Wednesday

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:56.510
get text messages from an unknown number on
her new phone from a number she doesn't recognize?

00:09:56.510 --> 00:10:00.779
Beyond that, why do those messages contain
new photos of Wednesday?

00:10:00.779 --> 00:10:03.978
Presumably this mystery will be solved in
a potential season 2.

